<title>GERMANY: German, French railways order 80 locomotives.</title>
<headline>German, French railways order 80 locomotives.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Bahn and French SNCF state railways have ordered 80 locomotives from De Dietrich Ferroviare, part of the De Dietrich group, and Linke Hofmann Busch, Deutsche Bahn said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Linke Hofmann Busch is a German subsidiary of GEC Alsthom.</p>
<p>The order will be split 50:50 between the French and German railways and the first of the diesel-powered locomotives, with a top speed of 140 km/h (90 mph), will be delivered in 1998.</p>
<p>The 641/TER series locomotives are designed for suburban and rural travel.</p>
<p>No price was given for the contract, details of which were published in the French press on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
